      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14267484/assets/fb86492e623d26711275e4637bdd29340dcdec2c175c30b8a5fb5df255a8170a.png)\n\nThe area of the quarter pizza above is $5\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}$, what is the diameter of the pizza?",
      "worked_solution": "The area of the circle is four times the area of the quarter section. So\n\n$$\nA=4\\cdot 5\\pi =20\\pi \\,{\\text{in}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the area of a circle is $A=\\pi {r}^{2}$, where $r$ is the radius. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 20\\pi  & =\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ 20\\cancel{\\pi } & =\\cancel{\\pi }{r}^{2} \\\\ 20 & ={r}^{2} \\\\ r & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\ r & =2\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{in}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the diameter of the pizza is\n\n$$\nd=2\\cdot r=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5}=4\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{in}.\n$$",
